{%- comment -%}
  Renders a product title with the U+FE0F variation selector stripped.

  Product titles on this store contain U+2122 (TRADE MARK SIGN) followed by
  U+FE0F (VARIATION SELECTOR-16), which forces colour-emoji presentation and
  renders as a grey box in a monospace face. Stripping U+FE0F leaves a normal
  text-presentation trade mark sign.

  Deliberately does NOT strip U+2605 (BLACK STAR, as in CRXST*RZ) — that is
  part of the product name and renders correctly.

  Usage:  {%- raw -%}{% render 'crooks-title', product: product %}{%- endraw -%}
          {%- raw -%}{% render 'crooks-title', title: some_string %}{%- endraw -%}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign crk_title = title
  if crk_title == blank and product != blank
    assign crk_title = product.title
  endif
  assign crk_title = crk_title | replace: '️', ''
  echo crk_title
-%}
